been playin for about 3 or 4 months now.
'twas my second ascension (first was valk).
 i'd been trying to ascend a wizard... got as far
as the plane of fire with one but got juiced by repeated
 archon interference :(. got another wizard as far
as gennehom, but didn't have a lot of stuff i wanted
(levitation, wishes..) so, i started a samurai for sh**s
and giggles. didn't differ significantly from my valk ascension,
except:

in the mines, genocided soldier ants... the scroll
was unidentified, i was surrounded low on HP, and had no method
of healing or any other recourse. my luckiest moment.

The evil samurai on the quest were *LOADED* with stuff.
i got 3 magic lamps from the top level store rooms, and it
seemed that every single ronin or whatever had a wand,
scroll, potion, and ring. i overloaded my blessed BoH and
had to drop my food!

The astral plane gave me fewer problems than my first
ascension, by that i mean there seemed to be fewer monsters.
i barely needed to zap teleport in order to get to the
altars (had to to go two of 'em). Ran into pestilence twice...
he made me ill and very ill.. thank my lucky stars my unicorn
horn did its work. the bastard kept dodging my /oDeath; took
me 5 zaps to kill him twice. Famine wasn't as tough, one zap
did it (thankfully, since it was my last charge).

All in all, a more or less easy ascension. I dual wielded FB
and katana from just after soko until i hit orcus town, where
i switched to silver saber to handle the shades. after i switched
back, i dulled my katana against a disenchanter (wasn't paying
attention...) and was running low on ink, so stuck with the saber
until got to plane of earth. had found a couple ?oEW on the way
up, blessed them and returned to katana.

a few things i'd never done before:

polypiling: after a lot of stuff piled up on an altar
on lvl 3, and a wand of polymorph was one of the
results, i decided.. what the hell. after an eternity
of zapping and rezapping, i got a couple of nice things:
gauntlets of power, multiple gauntlets of dex, =oConflict
=oRegen, =oLevit, =oSearching, helm of brilliance,
helm of opp., boots of water walking.
not sure i'd want to do it again to the extent that i did it...
not that i feel it was cheating, it was merely boring.
I always suspect a NH behavior when it becomes like doing
a chore.

killing shopkeepers (and wearing helm of opp):
during a polypile fest i threw on a helm of opp,
and decided to go ahead and kill a shopkeeper
to get that Firebrand i couldn't afford. he wasn't
difficult to beat w/ dual-wielded enchanted
snickernsee/katana.
After that, i got bloodlust and killed every
shopkeeper but Izchak. Spent the bloodmoney
on divine protection. One ill turn deserved another,
and i lost it by killing a gas spore near a co-aligned
priest. Woops. Eventually bought it all back though.

detonating a BoH: I'm surprised i'd never done this before.
i was playing very late at night (despite all good sense),
threw a /oCancel in there... Sayonara Excalibur,
sunsword, 5 ?oEW, 3?oEA, and lots of un/holy water.

No !oGE(?!?!?): i'm forced to assume i missed them,
but at the end of the game i had IDed all types of potions,
had never cancelled or diluted a potion i hadn't IDed, and
never saw a single potion of gain energy. maybe i blew up
a ton of them in my BoH... but i just can't figure how i'd never
see one after that. Chances must be one in an extremely
large number.

Foocubus dancing: The gods did however smile on my
succubus dancing. I killed all the ones i encountered normally,
and only found two sinks (but i didn't look that hard). The first
succubus hit me up 5 lvls, the second 2. The first abused my
constitution, but that was the only bad side effect.

Hit lvl 30: w/ succubus and gain lvl potions, and an uncommonly
abundant amount of wraith corpses, i was able to hit 30 in
moloch's sanctum. woohoo!

y'all have been great with the advice and encouragement.
i'd say this community is more than half of what makes NH great.

Now and always,
NHIAWOL

-jonker

